{"text": "Kittering Tierney Chartered Professional Accountants\nFile note -- HST audit, Saltfleet Marine Canvas & Upholstery Ltd. (\"Saltfleet\")\nOur file KT-0937        BN 84417 2290 RT0001        CRA case GA-2511-4470-9\n\nMeeting 14 November 2025, 10:00, at the shop, 41 Wharf Road, Bay 3, Dartmouth NS B2Y 3Z8\nAttendees: Lucien Arsenault (owner), Maeve Tierney CPA (MT), CRA auditor Priyanka Venugopal\n(Halifax Tax Centre, 902-555-0148 ext. 4417, priyanka.venugopal@taxcentre.example).\n\nAudit period: 2023-01-01 to 2024-12-31, quarterly filer. Payroll (RP0001) and corporate (RC0001) accounts\nunder the same BN are not in scope, although she asked for the T2 schedules.\n\n1. Vehicle. 2021 Ford F-150, plate GXK 418, VIN 1FTFW1E87MKD40193. 100% of fuel and repair ITCs were\n   claimed. No logbook. Lucien estimates 62% business. Auditor will allow 62% if he reconstructs a log from\n   the job calendar; otherwise she proposes 50%. ITCs at risk about $3,180.\n\n2. Personal charges on the company Visa. Two cards on the account: the one ending 3360 is Lucien's and\n   the one ending 2060 is carried by his wife, Odette Arsenault, who is not an employee. Auditor\n   pulled 38 charges on Odette's card (Costco, a Florida condo rental Feb 2024, her physiotherapy)\n   totalling C$11,942.17 on which HST of 1,557.67 was claimed. Denied under subsection 169(1) of\n   the Excise Tax Act. MT conceded. These also need to go through the shareholder loan -- subsection 15(2)\n   of the Income Tax Act exposure if not repaid by Dec. 31, 2025.\n\n3. Imports. Zephyr Sailcloth Imports Inc. invoices ZS-20418 and ZS-20455 (C$8,400.00 and C$6,115.50)\n   show no HST number. Supplier's BN per Lucien is 70219 5548 RT0001; auditor will verify on the registry.\n\n4. Unreported sale. Deposit of $23,000.00 on June 6, 2024 from Eastern Passage Yacht Club (EPYC) for the\n   clubhouse awnings was booked to shareholder loan. Commodore Dougal Fitzroy confirmed by email it was\n   a progress payment. HST collectible $3,000.00 -- included in the price, so it is 15/115. Auditor is\n   considering a section 285 gross negligence penalty; MT argued bookkeeping error, the\n   former bookkeeper was Lucien's sister-in-law and left in Q3.\n\nBank: Fundy Tidal Credit Union, transit 00417, institution 839, chequing 2204418. Auditor wants\nstatements for Dec 2024 and written confirmation that there is no second account.\n\nOwner details she took for the file: Lucien Arsenault, SIN 499 743 706, home 9 Shore Drive,\nEastern Passage, NS B3G 1M4, cell 902 555 0117.\n\nProposed assessment (auditor's draft, before interest): $7,737.67 plus penalty to be decided.\nNext: logbook and Form RC59 to Ms. Venugopal by 28 Nov. MT to draft representation letter.\nMrs. Arsenault to return her card. Fee estimate to client $2,400 plus HST.", "kind": "Text file", "detail": "428 words", "notes": [], "names": {"people": ["Lucien Arsenault", "Maeve Tierney", "Mrs. Arsenault", "Ms. Venugopal"], "companies": ["Kittering Tierney Chartered Professional Accountants", "Saltfleet Marine Canvas & Upholstery Ltd.", "Zephyr Sailcloth Imports Inc.", "Eastern Passage Yacht Club", "Fundy Tidal Credit Union"]}, "topics": {"places": ["Dartmouth NS", "Bay 3", "41 Wharf Road", "Saltfleet Marine Canvas & Upholstery Ltd.", "Halifax Tax Centre", "Eastern Passage Yacht Club", "Eastern Passage", "NS"], "health": [], "sensitive": ["owner", "wife", "employer", "bookkeeper", "SIN"], "names": ["Lucien", "Maeve", "Priyanka", "Odette", "Dougal", "Mrs."]}, "chunks": 2, "chunkErrors": 0, "topicErrors": 0, "importMs": 0.19999999925494194, "modelMs": 0, "topicMs": 35292.699999999255, "detectors": ["email", "url", "ip", "iban", "card", "card_exp", "cvv", "ssn", "bn_ca", "sin_ca", "ein", "card_partial", "phone", "dob", "age90", "date", "passport_dl", "routing", "credential", "device", "vin", "record", "account", "money", "street", "zip", "postal_ca", "places", "names", "sensitive_topics"], "detections": [{"start": 0, "end": 52, "text